lean-json is a clean-room reimplementation in Lean 4 of pydantic-core (its JSON parser and serialiser)
(https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-core), which is licensed under MIT and remains the copyright of
its authors.

No source code from the upstream project is copied here. Its test suite and
documentation are used as the behavioural specification, and each
conformance case in tests/Conformance.lean names the upstream test it
re-expresses. docs/traceability.toml records the upstream commit this port
was read against.
